const html: string = "<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"container\" style=\"max-width:760px;padding:0 28px;\">\n  <div class=\"crumb\"><a href=\"/blog\">Blog</a> <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/></svg> <span>Insights</span></div>\n  <h1>The guardrails that actually matter for customer-facing AI</h1>\n  <div class=\"p-meta\"><span class=\"av\">MA</span>Mariam Adel<span style=\"width:3px;height:3px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--border-2)\"></span>May 18, 2026<span style=\"width:3px;height:3px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--border-2)\"></span>8 min read</div>\n  <div class=\"post-cover\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0ea5e9,#06b6d4)\"><span class=\"pc-title\">Guardrails <span class=\"a\">that matter</span></span></div>\n  <div class=\"post-body\"><p>“Put an AI on our website” is easy. “Put an AI in front of paying customers and sleep at night” is the real task. The gap between those two is guardrails — and only a few of them actually matter.</p>\n<h2>1. On-policy answers</h2>\n<p>The agent should answer from <strong>your</strong> knowledge — policies, prices, docs — and cite what it used. When it isn’t confident, it should say so and escalate, not invent a refund you never offered.</p>\n<h2>2. Human-in-the-loop</h2>\n<p>Anything high-stakes runs past a person. A human can take over any conversation instantly, and the agent pauses its automation the moment they do.</p>\n<h2>3. Knowing when to stop</h2>\n<p>For a clinic, that means never giving medical advice. For a bank, never a balance without auth. Good guardrails are as much about <em>what the agent refuses to do</em> as what it does.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Escalate by <strong>topic, sentiment, and value</strong>.</li>\n<li>Scope <strong>data access</strong> and log every action.</li>\n<li>Test changes against <strong>real cases</strong> before they ship.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>Trust isn’t a feature you add at the end. It’s the shape of the whole system.</blockquote>\n<p>Get these three right and customer-facing AI stops being a risk you tolerate and becomes a teammate you rely on. That’s the standard GenuDo is built to.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"post-cta\"><h3>Build an AI employee for free</h3><p>Upload your content, connect a channel, and go live in a day.</p><a href=\"https://app.genudo.ai/auth/register\" class=\"btn btn-primary btn-lg\">Get started</a></div>\n</div></article>\n\n<section class=\"s white-bg\"><div class=\"container\">\n  <div class=\"s-head\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Keep reading</span><h2>More from the blog</h2></div>\n  <div class=\"blog-grid\" style=\"margin-top:26px\"><a class=\"pcard\" href=\"/blog/ai-employees-vs-chatbots\"><div class=\"pcover\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#4f46e5,#7c3aed)\"><span class=\"pc-title\">From chatbots to <span class=\"a\">AI employees</span></span></div><div class=\"pc-body\"><div class=\"pc-cat\">Playbooks</div><h3>AI employees vs. chatbots: what actually changed</h3><div class=\"pc-meta\"><span class=\"av\">YE</span>Yasser El-Sayed<span class=\"dot\"></span>Jul 10, 2026</div></div></a><a class=\"pcard\" href=\"/blog/whatsapp-team-workflows\"><div class=\"pcover\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0b7a63,#22c55e)\"><span class=\"pc-title\">AI on <span class=\"a\">WhatsApp</span> & Telegram</span></div><div class=\"pc-body\"><div class=\"pc-cat\">Playbooks</div><h3>Run your team from WhatsApp (without the chaos)</h3><div class=\"pc-meta\"><span class=\"av\">MA</span>Mariam Adel<span class=\"dot\"></span>Jul 3, 2026</div></div></a><a class=\"pcard\" href=\"/blog/cost-per-outcome\"><div class=\"pcover\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#6366f1,#0ea5e9)\"><span class=\"pc-title\">Cost <span class=\"a\">per outcome</span></span></div><div class=\"pc-body\"><div class=\"pc-cat\">Insights</div><h3>Stop measuring tokens. Measure cost per outcome.</h3><div class=\"pc-meta\"><span class=\"av\">YE</span>Yasser El-Sayed<span class=\"dot\"></span>Jun 21, 2026</div></div></a></div>\n</div></section>";
